# Mobile-first pages (hard rule)

Every **new or substantially changed** screen under `inertia/pages/` (admin, customers, marketing, errors) must be designed **mobile-first** and remain usable down to **320px** width. Do not ship desktop-only layouts and “fix mobile later.”

## Required patterns (use what already exists)

| Area | Do this |
|------|---------|
| Page shell | Use `<Page />` from `inertia/components/page.tsx` (responsive padding/title/actions). |
| List pages | `DataTableToolbar` + `InfiniteDataTable` (loads 25 rows at a time as you scroll, via `useAdminInfiniteList`); search uses `listToolbarSearch` from `~/lib/styles`. |
| Wide tables | `DataTable` + `dataTable.scroller` (scroll inside the card). Never use negative horizontal margins on table wrappers—they cause page-level sideways scroll on mobile. |
| Cards / sections | `card.base`, `card.head` (wraps), `panel`; multi-column forms use `grid-cols-1` first, then `sm:` / `max-[720px]:` breakpoints to add columns. |
| Page actions | Header actions must wrap; avoid single-row toolbars that overflow on narrow screens. |
| Modals | Use shared `Dialog` (full-width minus margin on small screens). |
| Admin chrome | Reuse `AdminLayout` (drawer nav ≤899px); do not add a second fixed sidebar. |

## Layout rules

- Prefer **stacked** layouts by default; add columns only from `sm` (640px) or explicit `max-[720px]:` breakpoints—not the other way around.
- Avoid fixed widths without `max-w-full`, `min-w-0`, or `w-full` on flex children (truncation/scrolling break without `min-w-0`).
- Do **not** use inline `style={{ width/height: … }}` for layout; use Tailwind or shared tokens (CSP-friendly).
- Dense matrices (permissions, variants): **horizontal scroll inside the card**, not page-level scroll.
- Touch targets: reuse existing buttons/inputs (already ~34–40px tall); do not shrink controls on mobile.

## Before finishing UI work

- Mentally check **320px, 390px, and 720px**: header, primary action, main form/table, and dialogs all reachable without horizontal page scroll (table scroll inside scroller is OK).
- Do **not** open a browser to verify; tell the user what to spot-check in devtools device mode.

## Hard bans

- Multi-column grids with no single-column fallback on small viewports.
- Toolbars with search + filters forced on one non-wrapping row.
- `min-w-[900px]` (or similar) on the **page** wrapper instead of inside `dataTable.scroller`.
- New page-specific side nav or duplicate layout shells instead of shared layouts.

Applies to new marketing/auth/customer pages the same as admin.
